    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="0659" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg653"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Baron
                            Ketteler.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-10-19"><hi rendition="#italic">October 19,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge, with
                    thanks, the receipt of your note of the 15th instant, communicating copies of
                    two communications from Her Britannic Majesty’s Government to the imperial
                    German ambassador at London, informing him of the concurrent intention of the
                    British Government to refuse its assent to the proposed ordinance of the chief
                    justice of Samoa making the registration of land titles held by foreigners in
                    those islands conditional in each case on a previous survey of the land, and
                    imposing a special fee for such registration.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
